       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is far above the maximum recommended dose of 200 mg per day for adults. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. It's also five times the ceiling, so it may be a typo. For example, 100 mg is a common dose.\n\nThere's another problem: I can only enter orders on behalf of clinicians. Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- If the intended dose was 100 mg (or another value up to 200 mg), a prescriber can confirm it and I can enter the order.\n- If you really do mean 1000 mg, a prescriber and pharmacist would need to review it directly.\n\nPlease ask the patient's prescriber to confirm the intended dose. I can then enter the order right away."
